implementationPlan.description:
DoD 4: the verification gate, run once. Run the verification command fresh: `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs`. On WSL run it as `env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs`, with no MOE_* variables (mem gotcha-local-runner-tests). It must exit 0; keep its output tail for complete_task. Then run the A-rows once under nvm Node 20 (v20.20.2) with --test-name-pattern='^A[1-6] ', to prove the test is safe on Node 18 and 20.
Mutation probes: run them in a `git archive HEAD scripts | tar -x` copy under your scratchpad, never in the shared tree, and use a replacer function in any string-replace harness. Each mutant must fail its named row:
- release after an unverified sweep (A5b);
- drop ifAcquiredAt or ifHolderWorkerId (A3);
- skip the pre-start sweep (A3, A6);
- a constant session id (A6);
- the caller's signal on lease calls (A5a);
- accept unknown input keys (A1);
- drop the busy Set (A2);
- release after a refused acquire (A2);
- skip assertNoMounts (A5d);
- treat empty releasedHolders as released (A5e);
- skip the post-end sweep after a session failure (A5a).
Report every survivor with its reason (equivalent or design-inherent), never silently.
Size: git diff --numstat against the pre-task base for the two files must total at most 400 changed lines. Comments and blank lines count, and no size exception exists. Aim for about 150 runtime and 250 test lines. If the honest test set needs more, say so in the step note; do not cut assertions to fit.
Leave peers' dirty bytes alone, and report every path you create or modify in modifiedFiles.

comments.content:
The operator approved this split in the architect REPL (2026-10-27).

R10 cannot be planned whole yet, for two reasons:
- its "owned attempt workspaces" are R09's guest materialization contract, and R09 is BLOCKED with no plan;
- it spans five concerns, so it would exceed the size cap.

New R10a (task-7988e5b97ea0484fae6bf8e49009266a, PLANNING, dependsOn R08) takes item 1 of R08's handoff: signal-safe guest job teardown in guest-supervisor.py relay().
- SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGINT kill and reap the job's session group, with a new fixed exit code.
- A SIGKILL of the supervisor still ends the job's session.
R10a is file-disjoint from R09, and R08 has landed code (b0e5982).

This row stays the final slice and keeps its full DoD. It now dependsOn R09 and R10a, and still R08 indirectly through R10a. Plan it once both have landed code. It still owns:
- the job table that replaces main()'s EX_CONFIG;
- running the agent as moe-agent (R07 already makes that identity with no sudo or groups);
- scoped provider credentials;
- fresh session identity, so that full context is forced;
- artifact preservation, and lease release on exit or crash;
- host-side kill-and-verify termination evidence in guest-session.mjs (R08 handoff item 2).
Expect a further SPIDR split at that point (job table and identity; credentials; reconnect). The R09 final plan defines the workspace layout this row consumes.
